Subject: [PATCH] ncsi: accept discovery deselect replies before package registration

Discovery sends Deselect Package to all package IDs before Select Package
creates their local objects. A valid successful deselect response therefore
does not require a registered package during discovery. Keep reporting
ENODEV for missing packages after discovery has completed.

Upstream-Status: Pending

--- a/net/ncsi/ncsi-rsp.c
+++ b/net/ncsi/ncsi-rsp.c
@@ -145,8 +145,15 @@
 	rsp = (struct ncsi_rsp_pkt *)skb_network_header(nr->rsp);
 	ncsi_find_package_and_channel(ndp, rsp->rsp.common.channel,
 				      &np, NULL);
-	if (!np)
-		return -ENODEV;
+	if (!np) {
+		/* Initial discovery deselects every package before Select Package
+		 * responses have created the package objects. A successful reply
+		 * to that cleanup needs no local channel state update.
+		 */
+		if (!(ndp->flags & NCSI_DEV_PROBED))
+			return 0;
+		return -ENODEV;
+	}
 
 	/* Change state of all channels attached to the package */
 	NCSI_FOR_EACH_CHANNEL(np, nc) {
